  "queue": {
    "filter": "abs(score) == 2 OR precedence_failure == true",
    "reviewer_instructions": "Read the evidence quote and reasoning. Confirm or override the score.\nThe extreme tiers (-2, +2) require strong, unambiguous evidence per Table 6.\nIf the model used \"supports\" / \"opposes\" language but the quote actually\nhas hedges, downgrade to -1 / +1.\n\nRejection cases:\n  - Quote doesn't actually say what the reasoning claims.\n  - Score doesn't match the rubric tier description.\n  - Wrong benchmark applied (use precedence_failure for §4.4 violations).\n",
    "routing": "2-of-2-disagreement-escalates",
    "conflict_resolution": "third_reviewer",
    "estimated_volume_per_week": 600
  },
  "compiler_notes": [
    "Methodology doesn't formalize a review queue per se — InfluenceMap operates a continuous QA process described loosely in §2.5 (line 220). Encoding the asymmetric review pattern explicitly so the runtime can surface it as a working queue UI for methodology authors who haven't built one yet.",
    "Estimated volume (600/week) derived from 30k evidence/year × ~10% extreme-score rate ÷ 50 weeks. Real rate depends on the LLM's willingness to commit to extremes; calibrate after first run."
